Let a later tail count replace a leading + count.
eat_num set the count-from-start flag for a count beginning with + and
never cleared it, so after a legacy +N first argument a later -n or -c
count was still taken from the start: "tail +2 -n 3" printed everything
from line 3 on instead of the last 3 lines.

Set the flag from each count parsed, so the last count decides.

---
 coreutils/tail.c |    7 ++-----
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

--- a/coreutils/tail.c
+++ b/coreutils/tail.c
@@ -101,12 +101,9 @@
 
 static unsigned eat_num(const char *p)
 {
-	if (*p == '-')
+	G.from_top = (*p == '+');
+	if (*p == '-' || *p == '+')
 		p++;
-	else if (*p == '+') {
-		p++;
-		G.from_top = 1;
-	}
 	return xatou_sfx(p, bkm_suffixes);
 }
 
